  "body": "The actual STEP bore spent 277.759 s in its release import/generate/verify test on the frozen baseline. With this change repeated release/debug tests pass in 5.866/31.308 s. Observed bounds on this Linux i7-1360P are 15 s release and 40 s debug for the complete test, including every growth level; these are measured bounds, not universal real-time guarantees.\n\nSimplify each growth opening's input at 0.25 um using iterative Ramer/Douglas-Peucker, erode an extra 0.51 um, and intersect the result with the original region. The intersection is the containment backstop; approximate simplification does not inherit the exact opening's nesting proof. Invalid simplifications or changed loop/hole counts fall back to the original outline. Load, travel and geometry budget limits and final path guards are unchanged.\n\nIndependent verification on Linux x86-64:\n\n- Actual STEP bore: baseline 15561/14837/1561 moves/planar-feeds/arcs; candidate 16029/15372/1427 in release and debug. The first candidate run failed only the old exact-count pin after its safety checks; only the measured Linux triple is updated, and the repeated release test passes.\n- Six planar adaptive fixtures pass: bore R12.5, rectangle and L-pocket unchanged; narrow slot stays HSM with 0 in-cut breaks, 14262 -> 14664 moves and 15.4 -> 15.7 % D load. Island and channel retain their named Offset rings fallbacks (100 % D and 42/40 breaks, existing fallback behavior, not HSM-law successes).\n- All six rotary fixtures pass with no new fallback/refusal: bar's deepest band 18.4 -> 18.0 % D, window's deeper bands 18.4 % D, neck bands 17.3/17.7 % D; no in-cut break over 5 degrees. Fitted arcs/move counts change; the Offset rings digest is unchanged.\n- Both annular-band refusal tests and all four motion stepped-pocket tests pass. Small-helix crossing regression passes. Seven new simplification tests pass in release/debug, including whole-region difference containment for acute notches, nearby components, thin walls/holes/nested islands, cyclic seams and degenerates. The 56 s debug growth-cost pin remains covered in the explicitly named heavy lane; the six defaults pass in 15.16 s.\n- Motion/app clippy `--all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` pass (271 default tests, 12 ignored heavy, 51 s, no VOID). Full release adaptive-unit run passes: frozen baseline 45 tests in 314.244 s, candidate 52 in 244.970 s, including budget twins and twenty slot perturbations.\n\nFull fixture count/load/break comparisons, commands, timing caveats and rejected alternatives are in the [decision record](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/issue/882-adaptive-opening/docs/decisions/882-adaptive-open-simplify.md). No safety thresholds are relaxed to accept a changed plan.\n\nLimitations: Windows/macOS were not run; their previously measured exact STEP triples remain unchanged and need remeasurement on those platforms. Graphify is unavailable on PATH. No snapshot or golden files change.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0, process version 52. The issue branch alone merges upstream main for the already-landed blockers; baseline tree equals upstream `4c229ed3`. Fork main stays on the released product baseline.\n\nChangelog: adaptive ring opening avoids repeated fine-outline offsets while preserving containment and safety checks.\nEffort: max; no escalation.\n\nFixes #882\n",
